Using polynomial long division:

Divide \( \frac{1}{2}x^3 - \frac{3}{2}x^2 + 0x + 2 \) by \( x - 2 \).

First term: \( \frac{1}{2}x^3 / x = \frac{1}{2}x^2 \)

Multiply \( x - 2 \) by \( \frac{1}{2}x^2 \): \( \frac{1}{2}x^3 - x^2 \)

Subtract from the dividend:

\( (\frac{1}{2}x^3 - \frac{3}{2}x^2 + 0x + 2) - (\frac{1}{2}x^3 - x^2) = (-\frac{3}{2}x^2 + x^2) + 0x + 2 = -\frac{1}{2}x^2 + 0x + 2 \)

