Next term: \( -x / x = -1 \)

Multiply \( x - 2 \) by \( -1 \): \( -x + 2 \)

Subtract:

\( (-x + 2) - (-x + 2) = 0 \)

So, the division yields \( Q(x) = \frac{1}{2}x^2 - \frac{1}{2}x - 1 \)

