The yard is a rectangle with dimensions 25 meters by 5 meters, giving it a total area of 125 square meters. The remaining part of the yard, which is a trapezoid, has parallel sides of 15 meters and 25 meters, and a height of 5 meters. The area of the trapezoid is calculated as follows:

\[
\text{Area of trapezoid} = \frac{1}{2} \times (15 + 25) \times 5 = \frac{1}{2} \times 40 \times 5 = 100 \text{ square meters}
\]

The area occupied by the flower beds is the total area of the yard minus the area of the trapezoid:

\[
\text{Area of flower beds} = 125 - 100 = 25 \text{ square meters}
\]

Each flower bed is an isosceles right triangle with legs of 5 meters. The area of each triangle is:

\[
\text{Area of one triangle} = \frac{1}{2} \times 5 \times 5 = 12.5 \text{ square meters}
\]

Since there are two such triangles, the total area of the flower beds is 25 square meters. The fraction of the yard occupied by the flower beds is:

\[
\text{Fraction} = \frac{25}{125} = \frac{1}{5}
\]

Thus, the fraction of the yard occupied by the flower beds is \boxed{C}.
