The triangle is formed by connecting these three points. For the triangle to be isosceles, two of its sides must be equal in length. Since all points are on the unit circle, the distance between any two points can be found using the chord length formula, which is \( 2 \sin \left( \frac{\theta}{2} \right) \), where \( \theta \) is the central angle between the two points.

