Now, the solar panel is flat but not parallel to the ground, meaning it forms a plane in 3D space. The heights of the pillars correspond to the z-coordinates of the vertices in this plane. So, if I can determine the equation of the plane passing through points A, B, and C with their respective heights, I can then find the height at point E by plugging in its coordinates into the plane equation.

