sqrt(10)*(x - y) = -sqrt(2)*(3x - y)

Divide both sides by sqrt(2):

sqrt(5)*(x - y) = - (3x - y)

Expand:

sqrt(5)*x - sqrt(5)*y = -3x + y

Bring all terms to one side:

sqrt(5)*x + 3x - sqrt(5)*y - y = 0

Factor x and y:

x*(sqrt(5) + 3) + y*(-sqrt(5) - 1) = 0

Solve for y:

y*(-sqrt(5) - 1) = -x*(sqrt(5) + 3)

Multiply both sides by -1:

y*(sqrt(5) + 1) = x*(sqrt(5) + 3)

So,

y = [ (sqrt(5) + 3) / (sqrt(5) + 1) ] x

Simplify the fraction:

