The set \( S \) must include all points generated by reflecting \( (2,3) \) across the origin, axes, and the line \( y = x \). This results in 8 distinct points. 

1. Starting with \( (2,3) \).
2. Symmetry about the origin: \( (-2,-3) \).
3. Symmetry about the x-axis: \( (2,-3) \).
4. Symmetry about the y-axis: \( (-2,3) \).
5. Symmetry about \( y = x \): \( (3,2) \).
6. From \( (3,2) \), applying the same symmetries gives \( (-3,-2) \), \( (3,-2) \), and \( (-3,2) \).

Thus, the smallest number of points in \( S \) is 8.

