The innermost part is \(1^9\). I know that any number raised to any power is just itself multiplied that many times. But 1 is special because 1 multiplied by itself any number of times is still 1. So, \(1^9 = 1\).

Now, substituting that back into the expression, we have \(0^{(1)}\). Wait, that's \(0^1\). Hmm, what's 0 raised to the power of 1? Well, any number raised to the power of 1 is just itself. So, \(0^1 = 0\).

