First, I know that time calculations can sometimes be tricky because we have to convert minutes into hours and minutes. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, I can divide 2011 by 60 to find out how many hours and minutes that is.

Let me do the division: 2011 divided by 60. Hmm, 60 times 33 is 1980, right? Because 60 times 30 is 1800, and 60 times 3 is 180, so 1800 + 180 = 1980. So, 2011 minus 1980 is 31. That means 2011 minutes is equal to 33 hours and 31 minutes.

Wait, but 33 hours is more than a day. Since a day has 24 hours, I can subtract 24 from 33 to find out how many hours beyond a full day that is. So, 33 minus 24 is 9. Therefore, 33 hours is the same as 1 day and 9 hours.

Putting it all together, 2011 minutes is 1 day, 9 hours, and 31 minutes. 

Now, starting from midnight on January 1, adding 1 day would bring us to midnight on January 2. Then, adding 9 hours and 31 minutes to that midnight time would give us the final time.

Midnight plus 9 hours is 9:00 AM, and adding 31 minutes brings us to 9:31 AM. So, the time would be January 2 at 9:31 AM.

