The harmonic mean of 1, 2, and 4 is calculated by first finding the reciprocals of each number: 1, 1/2, and 1/4. Summing these reciprocals gives 7/4. Dividing this sum by 3 yields 7/12. Taking the reciprocal of 7/12 results in 12/7.

